From 1ae0220db5ca9170012e89a75dcce81fb3838e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:17:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: MACRUNNER_FEX_HOOK_GUARD - no memory-hook
 notifications for FEX-internal memory inside invalidation

The r3 no-flush churn probe hung deterministically (wx-r3-noflush, 4/4 runs; span snapshot wxh-spans-r3-m1):
InvalidateGuestCodeRange -> InvalidateIntervalInternal (takes CodeInvalidationMutex exclusively) -> InvalidateThreadCachedCodeRange ->
LookupCache::InvalidateCacheRange -> the FEX allocator (rpmalloc) returns a 60 KiB span to the OS -> NtFreeVirtualMemory -> NotifyMemoryFree ->
InvalidateAlignedInterval(Free) -> InvalidateIntervalInternal -> the same mutex, held by the same thread (WritePriorityMutex is not recursive).
The ARM64EC ntdll wrapper only suppresses NESTED hooks (InSyscallCallback); calls made by emulator code outside a hook pass through.

Fix (default OFF; MACRUNNER_FEX_HOOK_GUARD=1): a per-thread depth counter in a Win32 TLS slot (thread_local is unusable in the FEX PE modules: empty TLS directory)
raised by HookGuard::Scope in InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked, InvalidateCallTargetPatch and DiscoverExecutableView; the Notify* hooks of that thread return at once.
Other threads notify as before. Counters by hook kind and the deepest nesting go into the macrunner-fex-jit line (hook_guard, hook_suppressed, hs_*).
The compile path (shared CodeInvalidationMutex in CompileBlock/CompileSingleStep) is NOT covered: the same class (upgrade instead of self-lock) is open there.
